%S A399201 0,1,2,3,3,4,5,5,5,6,7,8,8,8,8,8,8,9,10,11,11,12,13,13,13,13,13,13,13,
%T A399201 13,13,13,13,14,15,16,16,17,18,18,18,19,20,21,21,21,21,21,21,21,21,21,
%U A399201 21,21,21,21,21,21,21,21,21,21,21,21,21,22,23,24,24,25,26
%N A399201 Number of terms of A003714 that are less than n.
%C A399201 First differences are A085357.
%H A399201 Jeffrey Shallit, <a href="/A399201/a399201.pdf">Synchronous automaton for A399201</a>. The automaton takes k in base 2 and x in Zeckendorf, in parallel, and accepts if and only if x = a(k).
%F A399201 A 2-regular sequence. It satisfies the relations
%F A399201 a(4n) = a(n) + a(2n)
%F A399201 a(4n+1) = a(n) + a(2n+1)
%F A399201 a(4n+2) = a(n) - a(2n) + 2*a(2n+1)
%F A399201 a(8n+3) = a(n) - a(2n) + 3*a(2n+1)
%F A399201 a(8n+7) = -a(n) + a(2n) - a(2n+1) + 2*a(4n+3).
%e A399201 For n = 5 there are 4 terms of A003714 that are less than 5. They are 0,1,2,4.
%t A399201 With[{r = Range[0, 69]}, Prepend[Accumulate[1 - Sign[BitAnd[r, 2*r]]], 0]] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Aug 22 2026 *)
%Y A399201 Cf. A003714, A085357.
%K A399201 nonn,new
%O A399201 0,3
%A A399201 _Jeffrey Shallit_, Aug 22 2026
